# 6. MAKE DEPARTMENT MEMBERSHIP DETERMINE ACADEMIC ACCESS

The student's selected department or course of study must have meaningful consequences for academic gameplay.

The player should not be able to attend any department's classes and receive academic rewards simply because they entered a building.

For example, if the player selects a department in the Faculty of Commerce, they must not be able to attend classes belonging to an unrelated department in the Faculty of Arts and earn credits toward their CGPA.

## 6.1 Establish the player's academic identity

Save the student's selected academic information as part of the game state.

This should include the appropriate existing fields, such as:

- Faculty.
- Department or programme.
- Registered courses.
- Academic level or year, where supported.
- Class timetable.
- Academic progression and CGPA.

Use the project's existing academic data structures where possible.

The selected department must be consistent across the timetable, class activities, course registration, academic rewards, and relevant phone notifications.

## 6.2 Restrict credit-bearing classes to eligible courses

Only allow the player to attend classes for which they are eligible according to their selected programme and registered courses.

A student must not earn course credits or CGPA improvements by attending an unrelated department's class.

Validate eligibility when the player attempts to start the class, not just when displaying the class options.

If the player enters an unrelated department building, they may still explore it, interact with people, or visit a friend, but those activities must not be treated as attendance in their own academic programme.

If cross-departmental courses are deliberately supported in the existing game, allow them only when they are explicitly included in the player's eligible course list.

Do not impose an inflexible department restriction that breaks legitimate shared courses or existing academic progression mechanics.

## 6.3 Different interactions in other departments

When the player visits a building belonging to another department, offer appropriate alternatives, such as:

- Explore the building.
- Visit a friend.
- Talk to an NPC.
- Discover information about the faculty.
- Participate in suitable non-credit-bearing activities.

These activities may provide exploration points, relationship progress, information, or other appropriate rewards.

However, they must not award academic attendance credit or increase the player's CGPA as though the player had attended an eligible class.

Clearly distinguish exploration rewards from academic rewards in the game's progression logic.

