# FINAL OBJECTIVE

Deliver a polished, immersive university-life simulation in which the player creates a personalized student, arrives at the university in a detailed introductory cutscene, settles into their own accommodation, follows an actual academic timetable, attends eligible classes, and explores the wider campus through meaningful interactions.

The game should recognize the difference between the player's personal space, their academic responsibilities, and the wider university environment.

The opening experience should feel cinematic and welcoming. The character creator should provide meaningful customization. Hostel ownership should have practical consequences. Department membership should govern academic eligibility. Class attendance should depend on the timetable, and rewards should reflect what the player actually does.

**Implement these changes directly in the existing TerraSkills 3D project and integrate them with the previously specified campus redesign and transportation requirements. Do not stop at a visual redesign or a proposed implementation plan.**